  "notes": "{製作|せいさく} refers to manufacturing or producing physical goods. It emphasizes the industrial or craftsman process of making things.\n\nHOMOPHONE:\n- {制作|せいさく}: production of creative/artistic works (films, art, music)\n\nDISTINCTION:\n- {製作|せいさく}: physical products (machines, furniture, goods)\n- {制作|せいさく}: creative works (films, TV programs, artwork)\n\nNote: In film credits, {製作|せいさく} often refers to the executive producer/financing side, while {制作|せいさく} refers to the creative production side.\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {製作|せいさく}{所|じょ}/{製作|せいさく}{工場|こうじょう}: manufacturing plant\n- {製作|せいさく}{者|しゃ}: manufacturer, producer\n- {製作|せいさく}{費|ひ}: manufacturing costs",
